esigned to overhaul EU policies across sectors such as energy, transport, land use, and taxation, aligning them with the goal of reducing emissions by at least 55% by 2030. This package is referenced as a key pillar of the European Green Deal and forms the blueprint for member state actions and national strategiesâ€”demonstrated by Austriaâ€™s alignment of its photovoltaic policy with this framework [Data: Entities (250); Relationships (344, 345, 366)].   õğ<C   ~şşşııûûûıı½¿¿C~¿¿ïûûûŞ¿¿ßßßïûı~ß¿¿ßï÷şûïïïß4 şô-   Â 	{ @ €(XÀ ƒ "H˜@¡‚…2hØÀ¡ƒ‡ BˆA¢„‰(R¨XÁ¢…‹0bÈ˜A£†8rèØÁ£‡@‚B¤ˆ‘#H’(YÂ¤‰“'P¢H™B¥Š•+X²hÙÂ¥‹—/`ÂˆC¦Œ™3hÒ¨YÃ¦›7pâÈ™C§;xòèÙÃ§Ÿ?€	D¨¡Cˆ)ZÄ¨‘£G"IšD©’¥K˜2iÚÄ©“§O B‰Eª”©S¨R©ZÅª•«W°bÉšE«–­[¸réÚÅ«—¯_À‚	F¬˜±cÈ’)[Æ¬™³gĞ¢I›F­šµkØ²iÛÆ­›·oàÂ‰G®œ¹sèÒ©[Ç®»wğâÉ›G¯½{øòéÛÇ¯Ÿ¿ H° Áƒ*\È°¡Ã‡#JœH±¢Å‹3jÜÈ±£Ç CŠI²¤É“(Sª\É²¥Ë—0cÊœI³¦Í›8sêÜÉ³§ÏŸ@ƒJ´¨Ñ£H“*]Ê´©Ó§P£JJµªÕ«X³jİÊµ«×¯`ÃŠK¶¬Ù³hÓª]Ë¶­Û·pãÊK·®İ»xóêİË·¯ß¿€L¸°áÃˆ+^Ì¸±ãÇ#KL¹²åË˜3kŞÌ¹³çÏ C‹Mº´éÓ¨S«^Íºµë×°cËM»¶íÛ¸sëŞÍ»·ïßÀƒN¼¸ñãÈ“+_Î¼¹óçĞ£KŸN½ºõëØ³kßÎ½»÷ïà       Úä—LÂ    í@   Central role of the Austrian FedeXGovernment in PV deploy5   Scop=impleation:@ g@ buildings9HMandate is embeddedaa nAĞal strategic framework(   Legal and policy compliance…icA,s;   Technic0economP\easibility criteria dict‘rollou	İignific\for1¨â€™s renewable energy targets6   Potential 6repu)0al leadershipÄ¸benchmarkingR   Ã–sterreichische Photovoltaik-S-e as%¯ c-Ã p)!coordi)F hub!êHubert F!$er's pivot!uthoˆsubject-matter expertise9   Integra!ŞA-	a al infrastructure planning via Ã–NIPC   RMcHKlimamodellregionenËinnov%·Ãdemon%ÿion128?   Emphasis on>x  transformGflag%ipro×s'A±<trong regulatoryr lEU iã MnM0 ,A:logAI ,/soc!İLdimensions addressedE(5acceptA@$>   QuantiAve per¯$nce measure?`8milestone orien2<onJ   High-level6è0of research, a*force	­indiÕl d:opa§a„,Public engag}\ulti-stakeholder collabo